+## Addendum 2026-08-26 (on-target results, AGX Orin 64 GB / JetPack 7.2 / TensorRT 10.16.2)
+
+Two TensorRT 10.16 correctness problems affect `vision_1008.onnx` on this target and are handled by the updated
+`engine_builder` / `run_orin.sh`:
+
+1. TensorRT miscompiles the fused qkv-split/RoPE region of every trunk block **in every precision** (FP32 engine
+   cosine 0.57, FP16 cosine 0.07 against the PyTorch reference statistics recorded in
+   `assets/vision_1008.validation.json`; onnxruntime FP32 reproduces them to 4 decimals). `engine_builder
+   --break-fusion` inserts `Add(x, 0)` after each block's attention V tensor, which makes TensorRT FP32 match the
+   reference (rel-L2 0.002). The original FP16 vision plan built by this package (242 ms) is therefore numerically
+   wrong and must not be used as a baseline.
+2. Plain FP16 attention@V is numerically wrong (DART's documented failure). `--fp32-attention` pins attention@V,
+   Softmax and LayerNorm to FP32 (correct, rel-L2 0.049 vs FP32, ~466 ms).
+
+W8A8 result: `assets/vision_1008_int8.onnx` is a TensorRT-native explicit-Q/DQ INT8 graph (GPTQ + SmoothQuant
+weights, static per-tensor activations, block 0 kept FP16, activation Q/DQ on every block's proj input which also
+selects a correct FP16 MHA kernel). Built with `--precision int8 --break-fusion` (`run_orin.sh` default,
+`LQ_VISION_MODE=int8`). Measured against the FP32 (fixed) engine on 24 COCO images through text_c16/ground_c16:
+114/115 detections, identical-or-better COCO recall@0.5/0.75, GT mean box IoU 0.815 vs 0.817, no absent-prompt
+false positives; ~220–235 ms per 1008×1008 frame vs 466 ms for the fastest correct FP16 engine and 1055 ms FP32.
+The frozen "dynamic group-64 A8 plugin" candidate remains unimplemented; its onnxruntime-simulated quality ceiling
+is no better than the shipped static-INT8 recipe. Full details: `results/w8a8_20260826/README.md` in the project.
+
+### Update (2026-08-26, later): HuggingFace/DART export as the vision base
+
+`assets/vision_1008_hf.onnx` (+ `.data`) is the DART `export_hf_backbone.py` export of the same weights
+(bit-identical parameters; explicit Q·Kᵀ, real-valued RoPE, opset 20). On this TensorRT it is correct in plain FP16
+with no fusion breaker and no FP32 pinning (rel-L2 0.050 vs FP32, ~275 ms), so it replaces the Meta graph as the
+recommended base. `assets/vision_1008_hf_int8.onnx` carries the same INT8 recipe (~229 ms, detection-level parity
+with FP32). `run_orin.sh` routes: `LQ_VISION_MODE=hfint8` (default) | `hf16` | `int8` | `fp16`.
+Grounding class buckets `ground_c{1,4,8}.onnx` (exported with the handoff exporter, K guard lifted) run at
+23.9 / 95.2 / 190.1 ms vs 376 ms for the resident K=16 bucket.
